WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
The year is 833.

2
00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.510
A caliph orders scholars to say
that the Qur'an was created.

3
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.930
One scholar, Ahmad ibn Hanbal, refuses.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.270
He is imprisoned and flogged.

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.840
Behind the fight lies a deeper puzzle.

6
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.460
The Qur'an speaks of God's
hands and God's face.

7
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.740
Yet it says nothing is like Him.

8
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.500
So how do Muslims read these verses?

9
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.760
In this mission, you'll meet
three schools of Muslim theology,

10
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.450
and the errors each one feared most.

11
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.040
Then you'll compare how each
school reads the same two verses,

12
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.540
side by side.

13
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:39.100
Your mission: compare how three
schools read God's hand and face,

14
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.360
and judge between them.
